---
layout: base.njk
pageType: style-guide
noindex: true
baseTarget: "_self"
---
{#- Every element of the HTML living standard, what it is for, and a page of this site that uses it (to-do 8). The list is
    engine/catalog/html-elements.json; a build test checks each linked page really contains its element. The few with no
    content role elsewhere are shown live at the end. This page's head also carries the one <base> on the site. -#}
{%- set groups = [] %}{% for e in htmlElements %}{% if e.group not in groups %}{% set groups = (groups.push(e.group), groups) %}{% endif %}{% endfor -%}
{%- set link = "underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink-brand focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-focus" -%}
<div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-7xl px-4 pt-16 pb-24 sm:px-6 md:pt-24 lg:px-8">
<p class="text-sm font-medium uppercase tracking-wide text-ink-brand">Style guide</p>
<h1 class="mt-2 text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight text-balance">HTML elements</h1>
<p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg md:text-xl text-ink-muted">All {{ htmlElements.length }} elements of the HTML standard, what each is for, and a page of this site that uses it. The ones with no content role elsewhere are shown working at the end of this page.</p>
<nav aria-label="Element groups" class="mt-8"><ul class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">{% for g in groups %}<li><a href="#{{ g | slugify }}" class="inline-flex min-h-9 items-center rounded-full border border-line-strong px-3 text-sm text-ink hover:bg-surface-alt focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-focus">{{ g }}</a></li>{% endfor %}<li><a href="#live-examples" class="inline-flex min-h-9 items-center rounded-full border border-line-strong px-3 text-sm text-ink hover:bg-surface-alt focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-focus">Live examples</a></li></ul></nav>

{%- for g in groups %}
<section id="{{ g | slugify }}" class="mt-16 scroll-mt-24" aria-labelledby="{{ g | slugify }}-h">
<h2 id="{{ g | slugify }}-h" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">{{ g }}</h2>
<div class="mt-6 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-line" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="{{ g }}">
<table class="w-full text-start text-sm">
<caption class="sr-only">{{ g }}: element, purpose and where the site uses it</caption>
<colgroup><col class="w-40"><col><col class="w-72"></colgroup>
<thead class="bg-surface-alt"><tr><th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 text-start font-semibold">Element</th><th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 text-start font-semibold">Purpose</th><th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 text-start font-semibold">Used on</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{%- for e in htmlElements %}{% if e.group == g %}
<tr id="el-{{ e.el }}" class="border-t border-line"><th scope="row" class="px-4 py-3 text-start font-medium"><code class="rounded-sm bg-surface-alt px-1">&lt;{{ e.el }}&gt;</code></th><td class="px-4 py-3 text-ink-muted">{{ e.purpose }}</td><td class="px-4 py-3">{% if e.href %}<a href="{{ e.href }}" class="{{ link }}">{{ e.href }}</a>{% else %}<a href="#live-{{ e.el }}" class="{{ link }}">This page</a>{% endif %}</td></tr>
{%- endif %}{% endfor %}
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
{%- endfor %}

<section id="live-examples" class="mt-24 scroll-mt-24" aria-labelledby="live-examples-h">
<h2 id="live-examples-h" class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Live examples</h2>
<p class="mt-2 max-w-prose text-sm text-ink-muted">Elements that have no natural place in a company site's content, each doing its job here.</p>
<div class="mt-8 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">

<div id="live-base" class="scroll-mt-24 rounded-lg border border-line bg-surface-raised p-6">
<h3 class="font-semibold"><code>&lt;base&gt;</code></h3>
<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-muted">This page's head carries <code>&lt;base href="/en/style-guide/html/" target="_self"&gt;</code>: the URL relative links resolve against and the default target for every link and form here. Both equal what the browser would use anyway, so nothing changes; any other <code>href</code> would rewrite every relative URL and fragment on the page.</p>
</div>

<div id="live-style" class="scroll-mt-24 rounded-lg border border-line bg-surface-raised p-6">
<h3 class="font-semibold"><code>&lt;template&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;style&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;slot&gt;</code></h3>
<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-muted">A web component's markup kept inert: the browser parses it but renders nothing and applies no style, so the CSP never has to allow it. Script would clone it into a shadow root, where the slot takes the light-DOM title.</p>
<span id="live-template"></span><span id="live-slot"></span>
<template id="office-card-template"><style>:host { display: block; border: 1px solid; border-radius: 8px; padding: 16px; }</style><slot name="city">An office</slot><slot name="hours"></slot></template>
<pre class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-md bg-surface-alt p-3 text-xs [direction:ltr]"><code>&lt;template id="office-card-template"&gt;
  &lt;style&gt;:host { display: block; … }&lt;/style&gt;
  &lt;slot name="city"&gt;An office&lt;/slot&gt;
  &lt;slot name="hours"&gt;&lt;/slot&gt;
&lt;/template&gt;</code></pre>
</div>

<div id="live-noscript" class="scroll-mt-24 rounded-lg border border-line bg-surface-raised p-6">
<h3 class="font-semibold"><code>&lt;noscript&gt;</code></h3>
<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-muted">Shown only when script is off. Every page works without script, so the site needs it nowhere else.</p>
<noscript><p class="mt-4 rounded-md bg-warning-soft p-3 text-sm text-warning-strong">Script is off: the copy buttons, the count-up and the slider stay still; everything else works.</p></noscript>
<p class="mt-4 text-sm">With script on, the message above is absent.</p>
</div>

<div id="live-canvas" class="scroll-mt-24 rounded-lg border border-line bg-surface-raised p-6">
<h3 class="font-semibold"><code>&lt;canvas&gt;</code></h3>
<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-muted">A bitmap that script draws into, with fallback content for browsers without canvas and a text alternative for everyone. Nothing draws into it here; its background is the brand gradient.</p>
<canvas width="320" height="80" role="img" aria-label="Line throughput this week, rising from 820 to 910 units an hour" class="mt-4 block h-20 w-full max-w-80 rounded-md bg-linear-to-r from-brand-600 to-accent-600">Line throughput this week, rising from 820 to 910 units an hour.</canvas>
</div>

<div id="live-ruby" class="scroll-mt-24 rounded-lg border border-line bg-surface-raised p-6">
<h3 class="font-semibold"><code>&lt;ruby&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;rt&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;rp&gt;</code></h3>
<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-muted">Pronunciation over East Asian text; <code>&lt;rp&gt;</code> supplies parentheses where ruby is not supported.</p>
<span id="live-rt"></span><span id="live-rp"></span>
<p class="mt-4 text-2xl" lang="ja"><ruby>工<rp>(</rp><rt>こう</rt><rp>)</rp>場<rp>(</rp><rt>じょう</rt><rp>)</rp></ruby> <span class="text-base text-ink-muted" lang="en">(factory)</span></p>
</div>

<div id="live-bdo" class="scroll-mt-24 rounded-lg border border-line bg-surface-raised p-6">
<h3 class="font-semibold"><code>&lt;bdo&gt;</code></h3>
<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-muted">Forces a direction, ignoring the bidirectional algorithm: <bdo dir="rtl">Northwind</bdo> is the word "Northwind" laid out right to left. Use <code>&lt;bdi&gt;</code> to isolate text instead, as the Arabic pages do.</p>
</div>

<div id="live-u" class="scroll-mt-24 rounded-lg border border-line bg-surface-raised p-6">
<h3 class="font-semibold"><code>&lt;u&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;b&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;i&gt;</code></h3>
<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-muted">Not underline, bold and italic but meanings: <code>&lt;u&gt;</code> marks a non-textual annotation such as a misspelling, <code>&lt;b&gt;</code> draws attention without importance, <code>&lt;i&gt;</code> sets text in another voice.</p>
<p class="mt-4 text-sm">The operator wrote <u class="decoration-danger decoration-wavy underline-offset-4">recieve</u> in the shift log. <b>Mei Chen:</b> the line said <i lang="de">Werksabnahme</i> before it said FAT.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</div>
